    "path": "mobile-system-design/versioning-and-backward-compatibility",
    "figure": 0,
    "problem": "How does an installed app decide, at start, between the full app, a deprecation banner and a forced update?",
    "reading": "The app sends its version to the policy endpoint and caches the answer. AppPolicyGate compares the installed version with the two thresholds and chooses what the user sees; with no reachable endpoint it uses the cached policy, or OK on a first launch.",
