    "path": "mobile-system-design/authentication",
    "figure": 0,
    "problem": "How do concurrent 401s refresh the token exactly once, even when a caller is cancelled?",
    "reading": "Requests carry the access token to the resource API. On a 401 every caller goes to one TokenRefresher, which serializes the refresh with a Mutex, calls the IdP and saves the rotated tokens in the vault.",
