    "path": "mobile-system-design/telemetry-sdk",
    "figure": 0,
    "problem": "How does a crash survive the process dying and still reach the server?",
    "reading": "The crash handler snapshots the breadcrumb ring and writes the crash to a flat file before the process dies. On the next launch it is imported into Room, and FlushWorker uploads it ahead of other telemetry.",
